# Supplemental Figure Legends

## Supplementary Figure 1. Alpha Diversity Metrics by Person_Type

Bar plots of Observed (left), Shannon (center), and Simpson (right) diversity indices for Athletes (purple) vs. Non‐Athletes (yellow). 
Error bars represent mean ± SD, and “ns” indicates a non‐significant difference (p ≥ 0.05) for each comparison. These results suggest 
no substantial difference in alpha diversity between the two groups.

## Supplementary Figure 2. Training and Validation Metrics Over Epochs for the Deep Neural Network

(A) Shows the loss curves for the training set (red) and validation set (blue), illustrating how the network’s error decreases as the 
model learns. (B) Depicts the accuracy trajectories during training (red) versus validation (blue). Both panels illustrate the model’s 
convergence behavior and the tradeoff between underfitting (high loss, low accuracy) and overfitting (diverging training vs. validation 
performance) across increasing epochs.
